    "body": "For the ninth year in a row, the Pentagon has failed its annual financial audit . This year’s review covered $4.9 trillion in assets and $5.2 trillion in liabilities, with the department reporting incremental improvements despite falling short of a clean opinion.\nIn this episode of The Pentagon Buzz, reporter Ashley Roque reviews what’s behind the latest audit troubles, how much progress the department has made and why Pentagon Comptroller Jules Hurst believes a change in strategy could finally produce a clean bill of financial health.\nSubscribe to our Pentagon newsletter to get the latest information from the building delivered directly to you.\nBreaking Defense Video\nThe Pentagon fails another audit. Can it turn things around by 2028?\nWatch Now »\nA new Air Force stunt plane, plus a shakeup for special operations\nWatch Now »\nNATO nations have a missile crisis. How did it happen, and can it be fixed?\nWatch Now »\nA Pentagon impeachment showdown, plus defense funding in limbo\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nThe push to give dismounted forces direct access to LEO and MEO networks [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon wants a massive new military base. Where will it go?\nWatch Now »\nWhat now? Budget fight, Hegseth impeachment on deck for defense-focused lawmakers after midterms\nWatch Now »\nThe defense show circuit keeps rolling, plus Jimmy Stewart goes to war\nWatch Now »\nQatar’s domestic weapons, Turkey’s drone arsenal and the Mecca pact’s next test\nWatch Now »\n3 congressional races that matter for defense\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
